# The three-valued x < y of two intervals of the round-up interval: yes when xu < -yn, no when -xn
# >= yu, both false when an operand is empty (a comparison with a NaN is false); the default
# interval_less_1 on the meanings. Exact, in every rounding mode (docs/developer/design/upward.md,
# "Predicates and comparisons"). Requires the rounding mode upward set by kairn::upward::Scope and
# the options of docs/concepts/upward.md (GCC and Clang -frounding-math, MSVC /fp:strict).
kernel:        upward_less_1
rounding:      upward
input:         pair stored x = xu xn
input:         pair stored y = yu yn
output:        mask yes
output:        mask no
requires:      upward xu xn
requires:      upward yu yn
ensures:       trit yes no lt x y x=xu,xn y=yu,yn exact
min_precision: 1
source:        the lanes compared with the other lanes negated (the listing of the round-up interval)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_only:     yes
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the result is a mask, which has no non-finite value, and a comparison with NaN is false; trit states what comes out for every canonical operand

ny = neg(yn)
nx = neg(xn)
yes = lt(xu, ny)
no = le(yu, nx)
